# component: attachment
# decisions: A11Y-2, A11Y-13, API-16, API-28, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `attachmentVariants` drops `focus-within:ring-1 focus-within:ring-ring/50`,
#     and `AttachmentTrigger` drops `outline-none`. Upstream's arrangement is the CARD wearing a
#     ring on behalf of the invisible full-bleed trigger inside it, with the trigger's own
#     affordance silenced; this system has one focus affordance and it belongs on the element
#     that has focus. `rounded-[inherit]` on the trigger is part of the same hunk: the trigger is
#     `absolute inset-0` inside a `rounded-xl` (or `rounded-lg` at `size="xs"`) card, so without
#     it `base.css`'s outline would cut a rectangle across the card's corners.
#   A11Y-2: audited, NO HUNK. Every control in this file is a `Button` — `AttachmentAction`
#     defaults to `size="icon-xs"`, which is `size-6` (24px) exactly on the SC 2.5.8 floor, and
#     `AttachmentTrigger` is the full card. `attachment.test.tsx` measures both, so the day
#     upstream shrinks the action tier below 24px it fails here rather than quietly shipping.
#   A11Y-13: `AttachmentDescription`'s error ink becomes `text-destructive-text` in place of
#     upstream's `text-destructive/80`. Rasterised on `card` in this repository's tokens the
#     upstream pair measures 4.113:1 at 12px (axe agrees: 4.11) — a live WCAG 1.4.3 failure, and
#     squarely inside the 3.98-4.35 band `--destructive-text` was added for. A11Y-13 is not a list
#     of four components, it is the rule that a tinted status surface reads through the family's
#     `-text` ink rather than its fill; this is the identical pair Alert, Badge, Toast and the soft
#     Button already carry. It was never caught before because attachment's test lane ran unstyled
#     and `contrast.browser.test.tsx` had no attachment subject - a measurement gap, not an
#     exemption. Both are closed: `attachment.test.tsx` compiles the stylesheet and the contrast
#     lane gained the error card. `AttachmentMedia`'s error icon ink is DELIBERATELY untouched:
#     measured against its own composited `/10` tint it is 3.973:1, over the 3:1 non-text floor
#     (WCAG 1.4.11), so upstream stays verbatim there.
#   API-16: `"use client"` is ADDED. Upstream ships none, and this file calls
#     `useRender` from `@base-ui/react/use-render`, which calls `React.useRef` internally —
#     under the `react-server` condition that hook is `undefined`, so a server component
#     rendering it throws on import. `tooling/verify-rsc-safety.mjs` is what found it, the
#     same way it found `breadcrumb` in Batch 5. API-16 puts the boundary at the lowest
#     interactive leaf, and this file is it.
#   API-28: Attachment's widened scope (DS-44, approved by MK 24-09-2026) — file and media tiles
#     on any surface, not only chat. Five hunks:
#     - `AttachmentGroup` takes `layout?: "scroll" | "grid" | "tiles"` (default `"scroll"`,
#       upstream's row unchanged) and reflects it as `data-layout`; `"grid"` lays the tiles out at
#       listing size (MK 27-09-2026) — one, two or three equal columns, each at least 18rem and at
#       least a third of the row, so the counts match a `DataList` card grid — lets each tile
#       fill its cell, and gives the media a 16:9 frame like a `MediaCard`; `"tiles"` is the
#       compact form grid (MK 27-09-2026) — two square tiles per row on a phone, three from `sm`.
#     - a new `AttachmentProgress` part composes `progress`'s `ProgressTrack`/`ProgressIndicator`
#       inside Base UI's `Progress.Root`, takes its own full-width row in the tile, is named
#       "Upload progress" unless `aria-label` says otherwise, and announces `aria-valuetext`
#       "{n}%" of `max`. `value={null}` keeps the engine's indeterminate text. `state="uploading"`
#       without it keeps upstream's title shimmer.
#     - `Attachment` takes `muted?: boolean`, reflected as `data-muted`, which dims the media to
#       `opacity-50` and leaves the title and description at full ink.
#     - image media styles a nested `<img>` (`[&_img]` in place of `*:[img]`) and sizes a nested
#       `Image` frame to the slot, so the system `Image` with its fallback fills the media.
#     - `Attachment` takes `size="lg"` (MK 27-09-2026): a vertical tile is `w-40`, the listing
#       tile a product's files strip needs, and a horizontal one gets a larger (`w-12`) media box.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
